From f08e8a50799d923089cbec0b7bb5917c2b879191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The player's frame table kept while he uses it (SDK_PORT_3DS)

ov5_021EDB3C (is a frame table used by any object but this one?) read
v0 before setting it, on the first object: whatever its register held.
Built for the 3DS that was sometimes 0xffff, and then every object was
skipped: the table counted unused and freed while the player still drew
from it. Its memory went to something else, his frames were read from
that (his first start frames overwritten), and he stayed in one pose
whichever way he went, till the field was made again (the bag).

Now the object's graphics are read first, as ov5_021EDAB4 (the models'
check) does.
---
 src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c b/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c
index 48a3e35a..109fcda6 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c
@@ -1100,6 +1100,17 @@ static int ov5_021EDB3C(const MapObjectManager *param0, int param1, const MapObj
             continue;
         }
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+        // The DS's code reads v0 here before it's ever set (on the first
+        // object): whatever was in its register. Built for the 3DS that
+        // was sometimes 0xffff, and then every object was skipped: no one
+        // used the frame table, so it was freed while the player still
+        // drew from it (he stayed in one pose, his frames read from the
+        // memory given to something else, till the field was made again).
+        // As ov5_021EDAB4 does it: the object's graphics first.
+        v0 = MapObject_GetGraphicsID(v2);
+#endif
+
         if (v0 == 0xffff) {
             continue;
         }
